        <body>
            <div xml:id="d450">

                <pb facs="0877" n="753" sameAs="frus:frus1881/pg753"/>

                <head>No. 446.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Morgan to Mr. Evarts.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1880-12-25"><hi rendition="#italic">December</hi> 25, 1880</date>.
                        (Received January 13, 1881.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 144.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Complying with your instructions contained
                    in dispatch No. 80, I addressed a note to the secretary for foreign relations on
                    the 23d instant, a copy of which I inclose.</p>
                <p>I now transmit translation of note this day received by me from Mr. Mariscal,
                    from which you will perceive that Felipe Burnato, Santos Hernandez, Miguel
                    Guerrero, and Manuel Guerrero, mentioned in your dispatch No. 71, were dismissed
                    from the Mexican army in July of this year, and that Guadalupe George (not
                    George Cino, as the name was transmitted in your No. 71) deserted therefrom in
                    October last.</p>
                <pb facs="0878" n="754" xml:id="pg754"/>
                <p>I reserve pressing the question of compensation for their illegal impressment and
                    detention until I shall receive further instructions from you.</p>
                <p>I am, sir,</p>
                <closer><signed>P. H. MORGAN.</signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d450-a1.xml" xpointer="d450-a1"/>
